    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0807" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg521"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-07T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 7, 1916, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4144. Your 5271, December 5, 5 p. m. Department has never understood that
                    arrangements contained in your 4755,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d649-f1"/> August 22,
                    or 5076,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d649-f2"/> October 26, were intended to supplant
                    assurances contained in <pb facs="0808" n="522" xml:id="pg522"/> your
                        4661,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d649-f3"/> August 5, as to tobacco on high seas
                    or loaded and then awaiting shipment. So inform Foreign Office and make vigorous
                    representations as instructed in Department’s 4110,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d649-f4"/> December 1.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
